      "description": "Watch Panathinaikos vs Paksi SE highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 30, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as Panathinaikos and Paksi SE faced off in a high-stakes UEFA Europa Conference League encounter. Both teams headed into the match knowing that every tactical decision and individual effort would be crucial in their quest for continental progression. First Half Momentum The match, held on July 30, 2026 , saw an early physical edge as Andor Lapu of Paksi SE received a yellow card in the 11th minute. Despite the early pressure from the hosts, it was the Hungarian side that broke the deadlock. In the 35th minute, Milan Peto clinical strike put Paksi SE ahead, momentarily silencing the home crowd. Panathinaikos refused to go into the break trailing and ramped up their offensive efforts. Their persistence was rewarded in the 44th minute when Adriano Jagusic found the back of the net to level the scores. The half ended on a feisty note, with Janos Szabo picking up a yellow card in stoppage time as the battle for midfield dominance intensified. Second Half Drama and Equalizer The second half continued the back-and-forth narrative. In the 57th minute, Milan Gyorfi restored Paksi SE 's lead, forcing the Greek giants to dig deep once again. A flurry of substitutions followed, with Panathinaikos bringing on Facundo Pellistri and Rick van Drongelen to inject fresh energy into their pursuit of an equalizer. The tactical gamble paid off in the 86th minute. Elmin Rastoder , who had replaced the earlier goalscorer Jagusic, proved to be the super-sub by firing home the crucial equalizer. Despite late pressure and several changes from both benches, including the introduction of Barna Toth and Vicente Taborda , the match ended in a thrilling 2-2 draw, leaving the fans breathless."
